course: dictionary
lesson: 14326
title: Keeping the rules and customs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Observance is a noun. It means keeping or following something, such as a rule, a custom or a religious day. Look for the verb hiding inside it: observe, which means to keep, follow or notice. «Her strict observance of the library rules means she never runs inside.» Strict observance means following the rule exactly.
explain: In religion, observance means how believers keep their holy days and customs. «Many families take part in the observance of Ramadan, fasting during the day.» The clues are the religious words and the way people keep a practice, not just notice it.
explain: A third meaning is a ceremony or ritual held to mark a special day. «The village held a short observance to remember the people who died in the war.» When you meet observance, ask: is this about following a rule, keeping a religious practice, or a special ceremony? Then swap in "keeping" and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Observance means keeping or following a rule, a custom or a religious practice.
fact: «Observance» comes from the verb «observe», which means to keep, follow or notice.
fact: «Strict observance» means following a rule exactly, with no exceptions.
fact: «Religious observance» means keeping a holy day or practice, such as resting on the Sabbath.
fact: An observance can also be a ceremony or ritual that marks a special day.
exercise: «The club's strict observance of the rules kept everyone safe.» What does observance mean here? | Forgetting the rules | *Following the rules exactly | Writing new rules | Breaking the rules
exercise: «Muslims take part in the observance of Ramadan.» What does observance mean here? | Learning a new language | Playing a game in the park | *Keeping the religious practice of fasting during Ramadan | Buying food for a party
exercise: Ella says observance is just a fancy word for watching. Why is she wrong? | Observance means watching, so she is right | *Observance means keeping or following something, not just watching | Observance means eating a meal | Observance means shouting loudly
test: «The family's observance of the Sabbath means they rest every week.» What does observance suggest? | Losing a game | Running a race | *Keeping a religious day by resting | Cooking a big meal for a party
test: Which example shows an observance as a ceremony? | Lunch in the canteen | Reading a comic book | Riding a bike to school | *A quiet service to remember the day the war ended
exam: Which sentence uses observance to mean following a custom? | *Our family's observance of the harvest custom is to share bread with our neighbours | We went swimming on Saturday | The children watched the birds in the park | The bus was late again this morning
